WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.883 --> 00:00:03.112
Line 3 is a row of stations.

2
00:00:03.835 --> 00:00:06.563
Each station does one fixed part of the work.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.564
Lines and automation teaches you to design and improve lines with automation.

4
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:16.989
First the line itself, with design and robots.

5
00:00:18.086 --> 00:00:19.781
Then what keeps it running well.

6
00:00:20.498 --> 00:00:22.820
Error-proofing, variants and control.

7
00:00:23.832 --> 00:00:25.249
Last the business case.

8
00:00:26.565 --> 00:00:28.469
The first topic is Line design.

9
00:00:29.172 --> 00:00:32.005
You follow one carton and count the stations.

10
00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:36.703
The slowest station decides how fast the whole line can go.

11
00:00:37.725 --> 00:00:41.881
On a stack light you read whether a station is running, waiting or faulted.

12
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.076
The second topic is Robots.

13
00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:49.139
A robot is an arm with usually six axes and a gripper.

14
00:00:50.185 --> 00:00:53.424
A robot could place the cartons at the start of the belt.

15
00:00:54.497 --> 00:00:56.958
You teach positions with a teach pendant.

16
00:00:58.297 --> 00:01:00.213
The third topic is Error-proofing.

17
00:01:00.929 --> 00:01:04.226
The unit only fills when a carton stands under the plate.

18
00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:07.691
Two sensors see if that carton is there.

19
00:01:08.408 --> 00:01:10.707
Otherwise product runs onto the belt.

20
00:01:11.793 --> 00:01:14.626
Against this you use poka-yoke and an interlock.

21
00:01:16.014 --> 00:01:18.673
The fourth topic is Variants and changeover.

22
00:01:19.426 --> 00:01:22.061
A variant is a version of the same product.

23
00:01:23.099 --> 00:01:25.595
Changeover is switching to the next variant.

24
00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.840
While it lasts, the line makes nothing.

25
00:01:29.884 --> 00:01:34.284
For that the machine loads a recipe with settings like speed and positions.

26
00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:37.947
The fifth topic is Control and data.

27
00:01:38.704 --> 00:01:41.445
A machine has eyes, a brain and hands.

28
00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.797
Those are the sensors, the PLC in the cabinet and the actuators.

29
00:01:47.803 --> 00:01:49.788
You know the PLC already.

30
00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.780
Here you write the logic of the line as a ladder diagram.

31
00:01:55.076 --> 00:01:57.189
The sixth topic is Business case.

32
00:01:57.936 --> 00:02:01.605
It comes down to labour, volume, variation and quality.

33
00:02:02.626 --> 00:02:05.029
Investment divided by saving per year.

34
00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:08.229
That is how you work out the payback time.

35
00:02:09.273 --> 00:02:11.815
That is how line 3 runs automated.

36
00:02:12.626 --> 00:02:15.064
Then you move on to the numbers of the line.

37
00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:17.111
The whole map.

38
00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:22.464
Lines and automation is the fourth station of Automation and IT.

39
00:02:23.456 --> 00:02:25.743
Each of the six topics has four levels.

40
00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.372
Start at Basics level with reading a line.

41
00:02:30.062 --> 00:02:31.873
It shows where the rest fits.

42
00:02:32.906 --> 00:02:37.399
At Working knowledge level come line types and robots, sensors and changeover,

43
00:02:37.527 --> 00:02:38.967
safety and investment.

44
00:02:40.043 --> 00:02:43.120
At Advanced level come buffers and robot cells,

45
00:02:43.294 --> 00:02:46.591
choosing sensors, OEE and the business case.

46
00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:52.315
At Expert level come simulation and vision, error-proofing and sequencing,

47
00:02:52.408 --> 00:02:53.940
micro-stops and risk.

48
00:02:54.996 --> 00:02:59.141
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
